**Definition 7.1 (fixed reversible historical wire interpretation).** Use
exactly RCA Definition 12.4's canonical HistoricalImage bytes, including
the complete native event list, raw physical-state projection and actual
source/version/cut binding. For a target $h$ the target-version tag is
its actual old/main/bootstrap/raw-table phase. The package separately
binds the later service $D_1$ and activation chain. Fix $\Pi$ and the
layout of §§3–4 as public parameters of the structural runtime.

Interpret that wire value by the finite map

$$
\mathcal W_\Pi\bigl(\operatorname{Image}_{P}(h,Y(h),\mathrm{binding})\bigr)
 =\bigl(\widehat h,\Gamma_+(Y(h)),X_+(h),
          \mathrm{binding},\operatorname{bill}_\Pi(h)\bigr).
\tag{CSA.8}
$$

$X_+(h)$ denotes the same complete joint interpretations on this structural
storage. Decode the native wire fields, apply the literal compiler to its
finite event list, apply the incidence encoding to its raw endpoint and
use the same event/field interpretations. The bill is evaluated by §8 on
that event list. This is a wire codec for a structural historical image,
not a transmitted graph adjacency list or four separately printed view
lists. No service is asserted to execute $\mathcal W_\Pi$ at unit cost.

For a complete Call fragment, $\operatorname{wire}(r)$ denotes the entire
published/delivered result tuple, including its Image tag, package and
target fields. Let $\operatorname{payload}_{\rm Image}$ parse its
HistoricalImage field by RCA's exact framing. Applying CSA.8 means applying
it to that field; the enclosing result, binding, print bits and delivery
observations remain part of $Q_+$ and the actual Call response.

